1	# Anki MCP Server
2	
3	An MCP server implementation that connects to a locally running Anki, providing card review and creation.
4	
5	This server is designed to work with the [Anki desktop app](https://apps.ankiweb.net/) and the [Anki-Connect](https://foosoft.net/projects/anki-connect/) add-on.
6	
7	Make sure you have the add-on installed before using.
8	
9	## Resources
10	- **anki://search/deckcurrent**
11	  - Returns all cards from current deck
12	  - Equivalent of `deck:current` in Anki
13	- **anki://search/isdue**
14	  - Returns cards in review and learning waiting to be studied
15	  - Equivalent of `is:due` in Anki
16	- **anki://search/isnew**
17	  - Returns all unseen cards 
18	  - Equivalent of `is:new` in Anki
19	
20	## Tools
21	- **update_cards**
22	  - Marks cards with given card IDs as answered and gives them an ease score between 1 (Again) and 4 (Easy)
23	  - Inputs:
24	    - `answers` (array): Array of objects with `cardId` (number) and `ease` (number) fields
25	
26	- **add_card**
27	  - Creates a new card in the Default Anki deck
28	  - Inputs:
29	    - `front` (string): Front of card
30	    - `back` (string): Back of card
31	
32	- **get_due_cards**
33	  - Returns n number of cards currently due for review
34	  - Inputs:
35	    - `num` (number): Number of cards
36	
37	- **get_new_cards**
38	  - Returns n number of cards from new
39	  - Inputs:
40	    - `num` (number): Number of cards
41	
42	## Development
43	
44	Install dependencies:
45	```bash
46	npm install
47	```
48	
49	Build the server:
50	```bash
51	npm run build
52	```
53	
54	For development with auto-rebuild:
55	```bash
56	npm run watch
57	```
58	
59	## Configuration 
60	
61	To use with Claude Desktop, add the server config:
62	
63	On MacOS: `~/Library/Application Support/Claude/claude_desktop_config.json`
64	On Windows: `%APPDATA%/Claude/claude_desktop_config.json`
65	
66	```json
67	{
68	  "mcpServers": {
69	    "anki-mcp-server": {
70	      "command": "/path/to/anki-mcp-server/build/index.js"
71	    }
72	  }
73	}
74	```
75	
76	### Debugging
77	
78	Since MCP servers communicate over stdio, debugging can be challenging. We recommend using the [MCP Inspector](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/inspector), which is available as a package script:
79	
80	```bash
81	npm run inspector
82	```
83	
84	The Inspector will provide a URL to access debugging tools in your browser.
85	

